  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.outgoing_edges.fn` only says that criterion code uses the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.outgoing_edges` for this operation. The cited requirement therefore supplies the structural obligation, which is the method signature.\n\nThe implementation is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#2/fn[outgoing_edges]`, and it matches that signature:\n- It sits in `impl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D>`.\n- It is `pub fn outgoing_edges(&self, node: &D::NodeId, label: D::EdgeLabel) -> Result<Snapshot<Vec<D::NodeId>>, D::Error> where D::EdgeLabel: PartialEq`.\n- `Snapshot<T>` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[Snapshot]` has `content` and `fingerprint` fields, so it can carry the target IDs and the target-set fingerprint.\n- The body delegates to `prepare_edges` and `observe_edges`, and returns the snapshot.\n- `Domain::EdgeLabel` is `Clone + Send + Sync`, so the `label.clone()` call in the body compiles.\n\nThe function carries an `{impl}` reference to the `.fn` requirement. No {fixme} acknowledgments apply, and I found no structural gaps.",
